  "configuration_id": "config_004",
  "reason": "With only two completed experiments, we know RNA (pca_n2000, singleprofile) yields ~48.5% accuracy while image (resnet50, singleprofile) is much weaker at ~20.8%. The dominant uncertainty is whether the RNA representation quality can be improved. Config_004 (rna_only, singleprofile, scvi_n200) isolates exactly one variable from config_001: replacing the linear PCA encoder with a learned scVI VAE representation (both 200-dim), while holding profile setting, aggregation, and modality constant. If scvi_n200 substantially outperforms pca_n2000, it tells us nonlinear learned representations are critical and we should invest in richer encoders (e.g., scGPT) and multimodal fusion built on them. If it performs similarly, PCA is sufficient and we should pivot to testing multiprofile/aggregation or multimodal fusion. This single-variable comparison is the most informative use of the next budget slot given the sparse evidence."
}

